# Security boundary for image builds (Phytomni-Bot ships to
# customers). Plaintext secrets must NEVER enter the Docker build
# context; only the AES-256-GCM envelope (.env.encrypted, "PHYBOT01"
# magic) may ship. See README "Distribution to trusted customers".
#
# No Dockerfile exists yet; this file is intentionally added now so
# the security default is correct the moment one is introduced.

# Exclude every plaintext .env and variant (incl. .env.example) ...
**/.env
**/.env.*
src/mcp_server_phytomni/config/.env

# ... but the encrypted envelope is the one artifact that MUST ship.
!**/.env.encrypted

# Model A delivery: the per-customer license key is handed over a
# separate channel and dropped on the host at deploy time. It MUST
# NEVER enter an image (image leak would then equal plaintext leak,
# defeating the envelope). It does not match the .env* patterns
# above, so it needs its own exclusion.
**/.license_key
src/mcp_server_phytomni/config/.license_key
